# Judgment Escalation Ladder

**Invariant:** `seat_unsure ⇒ consult(independent_binder)` · `binder_unsure ⇒ consult(human_operator)` (rare).

**CDP operator-seat stuck (BINDING — operator 2026-08-03):** when the unsure seat **is**
`cdp/opus-5` or `cdp/fable` (operator-proxy), do **not** Cowork-Ask the human for judgment.
Transport: **`cursor-auto` → nested `cursor-sdk`** with `model=cursor/gpt-5.6-terra`
(default) or `model=cursor/claude-opus-5` (live checkout / premium; inform-then-proceed).
Human principal only for **true operator-only gates**. SOT detail: `cdp-operator-proxy`
blocked→ask **2b** · inv 19.

**Independence is the load-bearing property, not human-ness** (operator bind
2026-07-28 · `decision:gate-independence-not-human-ness`). A gate is honest when the
checking seat is independent of the producing seat on **weight class ∨ family** —
`independent(binder, producer) ⇔ weight_class(binder) ≠ weight_class(producer) ∨
family(binder) ≠ family(producer)`. Routing a judgment fork through the human adds
latency and zero epistemic value when the operator's answer is "consult Opus" — a
relay is not a check.

**Independence has two axes — weight class and family.** Either can carry a gate:

- **Weight class** — `cdp/opus-5 → cdp/fable` is a genuine check, not a hat swap.
  Fable is a **different weight class**, and the standing posture already encourages
  it "when outside perspective helps" (`anthropic-substrate`). In-family does **not**
  imply self-review.
- **Family** — crossing to OpenAI / xAI additionally clears **shared-lineage**
  blind spots (correlated error the whole Anthropic family may share).

Self-review is **the same model at the same tier grading its own output** — not any
two Anthropic seats. `cdp/opus-5` ratifying an artifact `cdp/opus-5` authored is
self-review; escalating that artifact to **Fable** is not.

**Substrate scope:** step 1 is **any cursor-family seat** — IDE lead, cursor-sdk,
subagents, and **`cursor/*` premium models including `cursor/claude-opus-5`**.
Premium metered Opus in Cursor is **not** the top of the ladder; it is still step 1.
When unsure, even cursor/opus consults **CDP Opus or Fable** (step 2) before the
human operator (step 3). `anthropic/*` API remains prohibited — CDP/Fable is the
web product lane, per `anthropic-dispatch-authorization`.

Operator bind (2026-07-28): the human is the permissive parent — intervene only when
necessary. **Lane entry, fork resolution, and routine orchestration are the fleet's
job** — cursor and siblings act; ¬ park on the operator for decisions the ladder
already covers.

## Ladder (binding)

| Step | Seat | When | Transport |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Cursor** (IDE lead, cursor-sdk, subagents, **`cursor/*` including Opus**) | Default — execute, orchestrate, dispatch | In-seat + `team_dispatch` / `Task` per `lean-context-dispatch-first` |
| 2 | **Independent binder** — pick a family ≠ producer (table below) | **Any** cursor step-1 seat is **unsure** — including when that seat is already `cursor/claude-opus-5` | Anthropic: **`team_dispatch(model=cdp/opus-5)`** · **encourage Fable** via **`team_dispatch(model=cdp/fable)`** (`project_ask` = escape only) · lane `agent_bus:6006`. OpenAI (code lane): **`team_dispatch(op=generate, seat=cursor-sdk, model=cursor/gpt-5.6-terra, contract=light-bounded)`**; **`cursor/gpt-5.6-sol`** for **targeted low-token** consults — per `consult-routing` + `claude-ai-cdp-navigation`. **`openai/gpt-5.6-*` API** only for **life / checkout-free** non-code (¬ code-lane default; `decision:code-review-panel-cursor-substrate`) |
| 3 | **Human operator** | True operator-only gate (credentials, irreversible non-revertible act, spend pause, IDE restart) **or** binders exhausted after CDP-stuck path (`cursor-auto` → terra/cursor-opus) still cannot bind a genuine *what we want* ambiguity | Cowork Ask / direct — **rare**; one question + recommended answer |

### Step-2 binder order (operator bind 2026-07-28)

Try in order; stop at the first that clears independence for the artifact in hand.

| Order | Binder | Independence axis | Use when |
|---|---|---|---|
| **2a** | `cdp/opus-5` | family (vs Composer / Grok / GPT producers) | Default step 2 — producer is **not** Anthropic |
| **2b** | **`cdp/fable`** | **weight class** (vs Opus) | Producer is `cdp/opus-5` (incl. its own output), **or** Opus is unsure. **Preferred before crossing families** — Fable is the in-lane escalation, not a formality |
| **2c** | **`cursor/gpt-5.6-terra`** (code-lane default) · **`cursor/gpt-5.6-sol`** (**targeted, low-token only**) · `openai/gpt-5.6-*` API only life/checkout-free | family + lineage | **Fable** is unsure, **or** the risk is Anthropic-lineage **correlated error** the family may share |
| **2d** | `cursor/grok-4.6` (≤ `high`) | family | Cheap breadth / third opinion; ¬ a substitute for 2b–2c on material binds |

`anthropic/*` API stays **PROHIBITED** — CDP/Fable is the Anthropic web product lane,
per `anthropic-dispatch-authorization`.

**Non-primary gate carve-out:** `lean-context-dispatch-first` §"Non-primary cursor
model gate" normally makes an explicit `gpt-5.6-*` bind operator-gated. Naming
`cursor/gpt-5.6-terra` / `cursor/gpt-5.6-sol` here as the 2c binder **is** the
standing authorization — fire without re-asking; still announce the slug + why.
**Substrate:** `cursor/*` = cursor-sdk (code checkout); bare `gpt-5.6-terra` or
`openai/gpt-5.6-terra` = metered API — ¬ the code-lane default.

`seat_unsure` (was `cursor_unsure`) ≠ permission-seeking on clear work. It means a
**genuine fork** remains after recon and the seat lacks authority or evidence to bind —
**regardless of whether the active model is Composer, Grok, or cursor/opus**.

`binder_unsure` ≠ cursor relaying every closeout. It means independent binders were
exhausted under sealed-unattended rules. When the stuck seat was **CDP Opus/Fable**,
exhaustion requires the **cursor-auto → terra / cursor-opus** leg first — only then
may a human bind (or an `ESCALATE` flag with `minimal_question` per `cdp-operator-proxy`)
fire. Human is not the first escape from a stuck CDP operator seat.

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Ask operator which lane to enter when spec + scoreboard already bind | Enter the lane; report shape on CHECKPOINT |
| Wait for Opus to ratify a shape cursor already built and verified | Inform Opus executed; continue on tick |
| Park on the operator for `manage` / `charter_reload` / manage quit-start / git-tracked implement | Seat executes; operator only on operator-only gates. (`charter_reload` = loop bounce only; charter-runner / manage recycle recipe → hub `services_ws.mdc` § Manage process recycle — tmux `0:0`, ¬ ask the operator) |
| Treat every consult as operator-gated | CDP consult is **autonomous** under `lean-context-dispatch-first` CDP trigger |
| Skip CDP and go straight to human on judgment forks | Cursor (incl. cursor/opus) → CDP/Fable first; human only when CDP/Fable flags `ESCALATE` or operator-only |
| CDP Opus/Fable stuck → Ask the human | `cursor-auto` → `cursor/gpt-5.6-terra` or `cursor/claude-opus-5` (`cdp-operator-proxy` 2b) |
| Treat `cursor/claude-opus-5` as ladder-top — ask human when Opus is unsure | Opus-in-cursor is step 1; consult an independent binder (step 2) before human |
| `cdp/opus-5` ratifies its own output at the same tier | Escalate that artifact to **Fable** (2b) — weight-class independence |
| Treat any two Anthropic seats as self-review and skip straight to GPT | Opus→**Fable** is a genuine check; 2b **precedes** 2c |
| Reach for `cursor/gpt-5.6-terra` before Fable has been tried | 2c is for **Fable unsure** or lineage-correlated risk |
| Ask operator to approve `cursor/gpt-5.6-terra`/`sol` as a consult binder | Standing authorization (2026-07-28) — fire and announce; ¬ re-gate |
| `team_dispatch(model=gpt-5.6-terra)` bare slug on code-lane bind | `seat=cursor-sdk` + `model=cursor/gpt-5.6-terra` — bare/`openai/*` hits API |
| Spend `cursor/gpt-5.6-sol` on broad open-ended review | `sol` is **targeted, low-token** only; `terra` is the OpenAI-family default on cursor-sdk |
| Default Opus/Fable binder consult to bare `project_ask` | `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` — `project_ask` = escape / IF6 only; missions pass `purpose=` on `team_dispatch` |

